The answer is a shortage of chicken.

771
00:34:55,820 --> 00:34:58,420
According to a McDonald's executive chef at the time,

772
00:34:58,520 --> 00:35:01,460
when the chicken McNugget was introduced in 1979,

773
00:35:01,461 --> 00:35:06,180
it was so popular, it led to a shrinking chicken supply.

774
00:35:06,340 --> 00:35:10,840
Helping franchises make up for this led McDonald's to create the McRib.

775
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:15,480
Whether you're having McDonald's classic crispy golden fries

776
00:35:15,481 --> 00:35:18,480
or a whopper right off the Burger King grill,

777
00:35:18,481 --> 00:35:21,480
it always tastes like it's supposed to.

778
00:35:21,481 --> 00:35:24,480
The reliable consistency of fast food

779
00:35:24,481 --> 00:35:26,480
is one of its hallmarks.

780
00:35:26,481 --> 00:35:29,480
In fact, when ShakeShack attempted to switch

781
00:35:29,481 --> 00:35:32,480
to fresh hand-cut fries,

782
00:35:32,481 --> 00:35:35,480
many people let them know how much they preferred

783
00:35:35,481 --> 00:35:37,480
the classic crinkle cut.

784
00:35:37,481 --> 00:35:41,480
But fast food also evolves, and at White Ciccar,

785
00:35:41,481 --> 00:35:44,480
The White Castle, the latest change is the introduction

786
00:35:44,481 --> 00:35:46,980
of the 1921 slider.

787
00:35:46,981 --> 00:35:49,980
Okay, so in the 1921, we're back at our griddle station.

788
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:52,980
Right here, you can see we have the nice beef here,

789
00:35:52,981 --> 00:35:55,980
along with our nice roasted onion there.

790
00:35:55,981 --> 00:35:57,980
So the onions are already a little bit different

791
00:35:57,981 --> 00:35:59,980
because instead of going raw onion

792
00:35:59,981 --> 00:36:01,980
and steaming it right in the grill,

793
00:36:01,981 --> 00:36:03,980
these have already seen a little bit of heat.

794
00:36:03,981 --> 00:36:04,980
Yes.

795
00:36:04,981 --> 00:36:07,980
The patty here doesn't have the same signature holes

796
00:36:07,981 --> 00:36:09,980
as the regular White Castle slider,

797
00:36:09,981 --> 00:36:12,080
Meaning, it has to be flipped.

798
00:36:12,081 --> 00:36:15,380
It's actually less efficient to make this.

799
00:36:15,381 --> 00:36:18,580
But what White Castle is losing an efficiency,

800
00:36:18,581 --> 00:36:20,880
they're hoping to gain in flavor.

801
00:36:20,881 --> 00:36:21,880
Take that seasoning.

802
00:36:21,881 --> 00:36:24,280
Now, this season is different than the other season we use.

803
00:36:24,281 --> 00:36:25,880
It is. This is the original.

804
00:36:25,881 --> 00:36:26,581
That's right.

805
00:36:26,582 --> 00:36:29,080
And this is the 1921 season.

806
00:36:29,081 --> 00:36:30,780
No doubt, also secret blend?

807
00:36:30,781 --> 00:36:31,481
That's right.

808
00:36:31,482 --> 00:36:32,182
Okay.

809
00:36:32,183 --> 00:36:34,180
The spice blend and roasted onions

810
00:36:34,181 --> 00:36:35,680
are not the only things different

811
00:36:35,681 --> 00:36:37,780
than the 1921 slider.

812
00:36:37,781 --> 00:36:39,880
The meat for this specialty slider,

813
00:36:39,881 --> 00:36:42,680
comes from a local premium beef supplier,

814
00:36:42,681 --> 00:36:45,520
but the original slider patties with the five holes

815
00:36:45,521 --> 00:36:48,020
come from a little farther away.

816
00:36:48,021 --> 00:36:56,560
We are here at White Castle Zanesville Meat Processing Plant,

817
00:36:56,561 --> 00:37:00,060
or as we like to call it, the providers of sliders.

818
00:37:03,940 --> 00:37:05,400
My name is David Rife.

819
00:37:05,401 --> 00:37:07,840
I oversee all of the manufacturing operations

820
00:37:07,841 --> 00:37:09,400
within White Castle.

821
00:37:09,401 --> 00:37:12,600
White Castle was started by my great-grandfather, Billy Angram.

822
00:37:12,601 --> 00:37:16,200
A lot of Billy's friends called it his crazy hamburger experiment.

823
00:37:16,201 --> 00:37:21,400
And this is where that crazy experiment has led the company today.

824
00:37:21,401 --> 00:37:25,640
At this facility here, this is where we take beef trimmings, grind them,

825
00:37:25,641 --> 00:37:30,040
turn them into those delicious White Castle slider patties that you get to eat in our restaurants

826
00:37:30,041 --> 00:37:31,800
and at our retail products.

827
00:37:31,801 --> 00:37:37,160
Currently, the Zanesville Meat Facility processes 650,000 sliders a day,

828
00:37:37,161 --> 00:37:43,800
3.2 million sliders a week and 13 million sliders a month.

829
00:37:43,801 --> 00:37:46,680
The whole process begins on our loading dock.

830
00:37:46,681 --> 00:37:50,120
We get shipments of frozen ground beef in five days a week.

831
00:37:50,121 --> 00:37:52,440
Trucks come in bringing us frozen ground beef.

832
00:37:52,441 --> 00:37:53,560
We unload those trucks.

833
00:37:53,561 --> 00:37:59,880
We put about quarter million pounds of beef a week through this freezer.

834
00:37:59,881 --> 00:38:04,040
All that meat gets thoroughly inspected before it's ground down,

835
00:38:04,041 --> 00:38:06,600
mixed, then ground down again.

836
00:38:06,601 --> 00:38:10,440
The slider meat is then pushed through a special mold

837
00:38:10,441 --> 00:38:11,480
to take shape.

838
00:38:11,481 --> 00:38:15,080
That meat horn is what gives it that wonderful square shape.

839
00:38:15,081 --> 00:38:19,080
Meat horn sounds like an edible musical instrument,

840
00:38:19,081 --> 00:38:21,720
but it's actually a sculpting tool,

841
00:38:21,721 --> 00:38:24,920
giving the paddy its iconic look.

842
00:38:24,921 --> 00:38:27,480
This is where we get our two by two square patty

843
00:38:27,481 --> 00:38:29,000
with the five holes in it.

844
00:38:29,001 --> 00:38:31,400
If you look at these five rods right here,

845
00:38:31,401 --> 00:38:33,720
that's what creates the holes in our paddy.

846
00:38:33,721 --> 00:38:36,440
The meat horn doesn't just poke holes.

847
00:38:36,441 --> 00:38:39,280
It also shapes the ground meat into blocks

848
00:38:39,281 --> 00:38:41,440
that gets sent to a freezer.

849
00:38:41,441 --> 00:38:43,080
They're in there for 20 minutes.

850
00:38:43,081 --> 00:38:45,680
It gives us the perfect crust, so when we slice it,

851
00:38:45,681 --> 00:38:48,480
we get a nice, even slice on our hamburger pad.

852
00:38:48,481 --> 00:38:50,520
Those slicers have the ability to slice up

853
00:38:50,521 --> 00:38:52,360
to 1,000 slices a minute.

854
00:38:52,361 --> 00:38:54,820
The finished patties get stacked, packed,

855
00:38:54,821 --> 00:38:57,660
and shipped out to White Castle restaurants

856
00:38:57,661 --> 00:39:03,060
to the tune of 156 million sliders a year,

857
00:39:03,061 --> 00:39:06,240
including a shipment that ended up

858
00:39:06,241 --> 00:39:08,000
right here.

859
00:39:08,001 --> 00:39:10,080
So now we take that slider press off.

860
00:39:10,081 --> 00:39:11,920
Oh, man, look at that.

861
00:39:11,921 --> 00:39:15,340
The patty has a char and a crispness

862
00:39:15,341 --> 00:39:18,480
that immediately sets it apart from the standard

863
00:39:18,481 --> 00:39:19,880
White Castle slider.

864
00:39:19,881 --> 00:39:21,680
We're going to add our cheddar cheese.

865
00:39:21,681 --> 00:39:23,200
All right, the smoky cheddar?

866
00:39:23,201 --> 00:39:24,200
Yes, it is.

867
00:39:24,201 --> 00:39:26,400
Oh, so good. One of my favorite things on the menu.

868
00:39:26,401 --> 00:39:29,740
Standing here watching smoked cheddar melt on a burger

869
00:39:29,741 --> 00:39:32,400
is definitely me and my happy place.

870
00:39:32,401 --> 00:39:33,900
Now, that's perfect right there, Adam.

871
00:39:33,901 --> 00:39:36,240
We can take those off and sign them on to our buns.

872
00:39:36,241 --> 00:39:37,240
Here.

873
00:39:37,241 --> 00:39:38,240
Okay, you got it.

874
00:39:38,241 --> 00:39:42,740
Throw a couple of pickles on, and then we wrap up these drool-worthy sliders.

875
00:39:42,741 --> 00:39:46,740
All right, I am going to show one of these to the camera and then show the other one to the inside of my mouth.

876
00:39:46,741 --> 00:39:54,740
So, Adam, what do you think?

877
00:39:54,741 --> 00:39:56,740
That was so good.

878
00:39:56,741 --> 00:39:57,740
I nearly ate my glove.

879
00:39:57,741 --> 00:40:00,240
I was trying to put too much of it into my mouth.

880
00:40:00,241 --> 00:40:05,740
It is, flavor-wise, the perfect hybrid between a White Castle slider and a one of my glove.

881
00:40:05,741 --> 00:40:09,040
lighter at a backyard burger.

882
00:40:09,041 --> 00:40:13,780
It has the char, the crispiness, the smokiness, even down

883
00:40:13,781 --> 00:40:17,320
to the onions and the cheese itself that I would associate

884
00:40:17,321 --> 00:40:21,300
with a burger at a family barbecue.

885
00:40:21,301 --> 00:40:23,800
But it has that unmistakable White Castle bun.

886
00:40:23,801 --> 00:40:27,340
It's really kind of amazing to see both of those flavors

887
00:40:27,341 --> 00:40:29,080
in one delicious package.

888
00:40:29,081 --> 00:40:32,380
It might take longer to whip up 30 of these bad boys,

889
00:40:32,381 --> 00:40:35,080
but man, is it worth the wait?

890
00:40:35,081 --> 00:40:36,920
1921.

891
00:40:36,921 --> 00:40:39,040
It's both the year White Castle was established

892
00:40:39,041 --> 00:40:41,420
and the number of these you'll want to eat.

893
00:40:41,421 --> 00:40:43,540
My shift is over, my belly is full,

894
00:40:43,541 --> 00:40:46,120
and we got an exclusive peep behind the curtain

895
00:40:46,121 --> 00:40:49,940
at two of the fast food industry's titans.

896
00:40:49,941 --> 00:40:52,760
From the world of burgers to the world of fried chicken,

897
00:40:52,761 --> 00:40:55,760
from working the line at the legendary White Castle

898
00:40:55,761 --> 00:40:59,520
to finding out why KFC is an international phenomenon.

899
00:40:59,521 --> 00:41:01,620
You can't tell the story of American food

900
00:41:01,621 --> 00:41:04,520
without also telling the story of the fast food chains

901
00:41:04,521 --> 00:41:08,160
and restaurants that help build and define it.

902
00:41:08,161 --> 00:41:10,600
So the next time you grab your burger, your fry,

903
00:41:10,601 --> 00:41:13,520
remember, there's a lot of hard work, ingenuity,

904
00:41:13,521 --> 00:41:16,500
and technology to keep it at a fair price.

905
00:41:16,501 --> 00:41:18,740
And of course, fast.

